      "id": "sol.amc-8-1993-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring: \\(39 = 3 \\times 13,\\) \\(51 = 3 \\times 17,\\) \\(77 = 7 \\times 11,\\) \\(91 = 7 \\times 13,\\) and \\(121 = 11 \\times 11.\\)\n\nThe largest prime factor among these is \\(17,\\) which is a factor of \\(51.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B .",
      "hints": [
        "Factor each number completely into primes",
        "Compare the largest prime in each factorization; note \\(51 = 3 \\times 17\\)"
      ],
